Abbreviation_in_the_article":"Complex 2","Cell_line":"NIH-3T3","Time(h)":24,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"282.37 ± 2.16","IC50_Dark_value":282.37,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1002/aoc.7574","Year":2024,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-040517","value":"117.88 ± 1.12","numeric":117.88}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Complex 2","value":1.53,"value_relation":"=","std":0.06,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1002/aoc.7574","year":2024,"record_id":"MLDB-004563","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicity of complexes 1-3 was determined by the “shake flask” method betweenoctanol/water phase partitions. Octanol-saturated water (OSW) and water-saturated octanol (WSO) were prepared using analytical grade octanol (Sigma Aldrich) and doubly distilled water. Complexes 1-3 (1 mg/mL; ethanol/water 1/6) were diluted to 2, 4, 6, 8, and 10 μg/mL in water; alternatively these (1 mg/mL) were diluted to 2, 4, 6, 8, and 10 μg/mL in octanol, respectively.Appropriate amounts of the complexes (4 mg/mL) were shaken for 24 h at room temperature in equal volume (50/50). After the attainment of equilibrium, the organic and aqueous phases were separated and centrifuged. Finally, the concentration of the drug in each phase was determined by UV-vis spectroscopy. The sample solution concentration was used to calculate log P. Partition coefficients for complexes 1-3 were calculated using the equation log P = log[(1-3)oct/(1-3)aq].5"}]}